      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think aosp/4368076 already does all of this. Right after these checks, `io_uring_setup()` (through `io_uring_allowed()`), `io_uring_enter()` and `io_uring_register()` already fail with `-EPERM` for a 4KB mm, and `io_uring_get_unmapped_area()` and `io_uring_mmap()` refuse to map a ring with `-EOPNOTSUPP`. The `io_uring_enter()` check is there for a ring passed on by a native process, which is the case `io_uring_mmap_ppps.c` tests.\n\nSince the new checks run first, the only changes are `-EOPNOTSUPP` instead of `-EPERM` and no `p3s_4k_unsupported()` log. `-EPERM` is what `io_uring_allowed()` returns when `io_uring_disabled` is set, so callers that already cope with a disabled io_uring get the same error.\n\nWould it be OK to drop this patch, and have `io_uring_mmap_ppps.c` in aosp/4367986 expect `EPERM` from setup, enter and register?",
